import type { ServiceNotes } from './types';

// Platform-service local substance.
//
// THE PROBLEM THIS FIELD SOLVES FOR PLATFORM PAGES
// A booking platform's rules, fees and ranking behavior are identical in
// Kennesaw and Dunwoody. So nothing below claims that Vrbo, a direct channel or
// Homes & Villas "works differently" in a given city — that would be false, and
// it is exactly the padding an audit would (correctly) recommend deleting.
//
// What genuinely varies by city is the PROPERTY and the GUEST: what the housing
// stock actually is, who travels there and why, and therefore which channel
// suits that pair. Every entry below is written on that axis, and several say
// plainly where the honest answer is "probably not this channel".
//
// COMPLIANCE (do not remove):
//  - No claim, anywhere, that ATLStay is an approved, select or partnered
//    Homes & Villas by Marriott Bonvoy property manager. Marriott publishes no
//    such relationship for us and none is implied.
//  - No commission figure for the Homes & Villas program (Marriott publishes
//    none). Platform fee mechanics live on the service hub, not repeated here.
//  - No TripAdvisor / FlipKey as a distribution channel — that marketplace was
//    terminated in November 2025.
//  - No Google Vacation Rentals pitch — individual homeowners are ineligible.
//  - No figure for OUR management rate; that renders from config via feeLine().
//
